    "axis": "clarity",
    "evidence": "The headline, instruction, control grouping, prominent LAUNCH EVENT CTA, side-by-side ALLOW/BLOCK result, and explanation list make the basic task understandable across viewports. However, the result artifact never restates the submitted event configuration, so “same event” is asserted rather than visibly demonstrated. Specialized labels such as TTL, fan-out, fused risk, and evidence layers are also unexplained, while mobile requires a long scroll from action to outcome.",
    "fix": "Add a compact submitted-event summary beside the results showing the exact selected and changed inputs, plus brief definitions or tooltips for specialist metrics. On mobile, keep a short event summary visible at the result boundary so the comparison remains attributable without presenter explanation.",
